 te-change\nSign-up needed\nDate/time: \n\n Friday 20 November 2026 \n\n 4:
 00pm to 5:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n David Attenborough Building\n\n About \n
 \n Speaker: Elbert de Jong (Full Professor of Private Law at Utrecht Unive
 rsity\, The Netherlands)\n Climate change is rapidly entering the domain o
 f tort law. This development is driven by regulation and litigation\, adva
 nces in climate science\, and the increasingly tangible impacts of climate
  change on interests protected by private law.\n With a focus on European 
 jurisdictions\, this seminar examines the doctrinal and institutional chal
 lenges involved in developing and allocating climate change-related respon
 sibility and liability among private actors.\n The Cambridge Seminar Serie
 s on Law and the Climate Crisis explores the vital role of legal systems i
 n tackling one of the most pressing issues of our time.\n This series brin
 gs together top experts in law and climate action to discus
END:VEVENT
