 ding\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Dr Rupert Stuart-Smith (Deputy Director and S
 enior Research Fellow in Climate Science and the Law at the Oxford Sustain
 able Law Programme\, University of Oxford)\n Two decades of attribution re
 search have shed light on the impacts of climate change occurring worldwid
 e. The first wave of attribution research quantified climate change impact
 s on the intensity and probability of extreme weather events and slow-onse
 t changes in glaciers and sea levels. Over the past decade\, impact attrib
 ution studies have extended these methods to assess the attributable impac
 ts of extreme events on agriculture\, health\, economic losses and biodive
 rsity. Concurrently\, source attribution research quantified individual em
 itters’ contributions to climate change impacts.\n Steady progress towar
 ds 
